---
import catalog from '../../data/45north.json';
import instrument from '../../data/45north-survey.json';
import { profile } from '../../data/profile';
import IssueRatingRow from '../../components/IssueRatingRow.astro';
import { makeGroups } from '../../../public/45north/assets/groups.mjs';

const title = '45 North · Rate the Top 45 — Drew Cleaver';
const description = 'Rate 45 issues from 1 to 10 and put the five issues in each topic in your own priority order.';
const canonical = new URL('/45north/', profile.website).href;
const api = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_45NORTH_API ?? 'https://forty-five-north-api.drewcleaver.chatgpt.site';
const preview = ['1', 'true'].includes(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_45NORTH_PREVIEW ?? '');
const wording = new Map(instrument.map(issue => [issue.id, issue]));
const seed = catalog.map(issue => ({...issue, ...wording.get(issue.id)}))
  .sort((a, b) => a.title.localeCompare(b.title, 'en'));
const groups = makeGroups(seed, seed.map(idea => idea.id)).sort((a,b) => a.label.localeCompare(b.label, 'en'));
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#193f35" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="45 North · Rate the Top 45" />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/45north/assets/issue-list.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/45north/assets/issue-list-results.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/45north/assets/grouped-list.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/45north/assets/group-order.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div id="north-app" data-north data-api={api} data-email={profile.email} data-preview={preview ? 'true' : undefined}>
      <header class="masthead">
        <div class="wrap masthead-inner">
          <a class="north-mark" href="/45north/" aria-label="45 North home"><span class="direction" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>45</strong> North</span></a>
          <label class="topic-jump" id="topic-jump-label">
            <span class="sr-only">Jump to a topic</span>
            <select id="topic-jump" disabled>
              <option value="">Topics</option>
              {groups.map(group => <option value={group.id}>{group.label}</option>)}
            </select>
          </label>
          <details class="suggest-panel" id="suggest-panel">
            <summary><span class="add" aria-hidden="true">+</span> <span>Suggest<span class="suggest-object"> an issue</span></span></summary>
            <form id="suggest-form" class="suggest-form">
              <label for="suggest-text">What would you change?</label>
              <p class="form-hint" id="suggest-hint">One sentence is enough. Leave out personal details.</p>
              <textarea id="suggest-text" name="text" required maxlength="500" rows="3" aria-describedby="suggest-hint"></textarea>
              <div data-role="matches" class="form-matches"></div>
              <button type="submit" class="primary-action" disabled>Send suggestion</button>
              <div data-role="form-result" aria-live="polite" class="form-result"></div>
            </form>
          </details>
        </div>
      </header>
      {preview && <p class="wrap preview-note">Owner-only rehearsal. Everyone here shares one test connection.</p>}
      <main class="wrap" id="main" tabindex="-1">
        <section id="list-view" aria-labelledby="list-title">
          <div class="intro">
            <div class="intro-copy">
              <h1 id="list-title" tabindex="-1">Rate the Top <em id="list-count">{Math.min(45, seed.length)}</em></h1>
              <p class="priority-question" id="rating-question">How much of a priority should this change be in your community?</p>
              <p class="intro-hint">Rate any issue. You can also rank five within a topic.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="scale-key" id="scale-anchors"><span><strong>1</strong> Lowest priority</span><span class="scale-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>10</strong> Highest priority</span></p>
            <span id="rating-label" class="sr-only">Priority rating for</span>
          </div>
          <div class="list-toolbar">
            <label class="search-box" for="search"><span class="search-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sr-only">Find an issue by words, topic or issue number</span><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Find an issue" autocomplete="off" /></label>
            <label class="result-switch"><input id="show-results" type="checkbox" aria-controls="results-tools group-results-tools issue-list" /> <span>Show community results</span></label>
          </div>
          <div id="results-tools" hidden></div>
          <div id="group-results-tools" hidden></div>
          <div class="list-status">
            <p class="privacy-short">{preview ? 'On the public survey · ' : ''}No account, cookies or ad tracking.</p>
            <p id="search-summary" class="search-summary" role="status"></p>
            <a href="#suggest" id="search-suggest" hidden>Suggest this issue</a>
          </div>
          <p id="catalog-notice" role="status" hidden></p>
          <noscript><p class="noscript">You can read all nine groups here. Enable JavaScript to rate an issue, rank a group, or view live results.</p></noscript>
          <div id="issue-list" class="issue-list grouped-list">
            {groups.map(group => (
              <section class="priority-group" data-group-id={group.id} aria-labelledby={`group-${group.id}`}>
                <header class="group-heading">
                  <h2 id={`group-${group.id}`} data-group-title tabindex="-1">{group.label}</h2>
                  <a data-order-jump href={`#order-${group.id}`} aria-label={`Rank these five in ${group.label}`}>Rank these five <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
                </header>
                <div data-group-rows>
                  {seed.filter(idea => group.ids.includes(idea.id)).map(idea => <IssueRatingRow idea={idea} />)}
                </div>
                <div id={`order-${group.id}`} data-group-editor data-group-order tabindex="-1">
                  <p class="initial-rank-note">Choose the order you would address these five issues.</p>
                  <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to save an order.</p></noscript>
                </div>
              </section>
            ))}
            <section class="other-group" id="other-group" aria-labelledby="other-heading" hidden>
              <header class="group-heading"><h2 id="other-heading">Other issues</h2></header>
              <div data-other-rows></div>
            </section>
            <section class="matching-issues" id="matching-issues" aria-labelledby="matching-heading" hidden>
              <header class="group-heading">
                <h2 id="matching-heading">Matching issues</h2>
                <button class="back-to-groups" type="button" data-back-to-groups>Back to groups</button>
              </header>
              <div data-matching-rows></div>
            </section>
          </div>
          <script is:inline>
            // Shuffle groups and their individual issues independently before the survey becomes interactive.
            (() => {
              const list = document.getElementById('issue-list');
              function shuffle(nodes) {
                for (let i = nodes.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
                  const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
                  [nodes[i], nodes[j]] = [nodes[j], nodes[i]];
                }
                return nodes;
              }
              const end = document.getElementById('other-group');
              for (const section of shuffle(Array.from(list.querySelectorAll('[data-group-id]')))) {
                const holder = section.querySelector('[data-group-rows]');
                holder.append(...shuffle(Array.from(holder.children)));
                list.insertBefore(section, end);
              }
              list.dataset.shuffled = 'true';
            })();
          </script>
          <template id="issue-row-template"><IssueRatingRow /></template>
          <button type="button" class="secondary-action more-issues" id="more-issues" hidden>Show other issues</button>
          <section class="guide" aria-label="About this survey">
            <details id="survey-method">
              <summary>How ratings work</summary>
              <p>Each issue uses the same 1–10 scale. You can give several changes the same score, leave an issue unrated, or change a rating. A low score can mean other needs come first.</p>
              <p>The nine topics and the issues in each topic are shuffled for each visit. If more than 45 issues are active, the Top 45 are selected by median priority, then number of ratings, then permanent issue number. Unrated issues follow rated issues. Search or show other issues to reach the rest.</p>
              <p>Ranking a topic is optional. First means the issue you would take up first among those five. Fifth means the one you would take up last among them. You can rate all five issues 10 and still give them different positions. Each complete order counts once for its exact group of five. A changed group starts its own comparison.</p>
              <p>Each public connection can hold one current rating per issue. A new rating or a change counts for 30 days. Repeating the same number keeps its expiry. Open an issue’s details to remove a rating. A saved group order also lasts 30 days. You can revise or remove it in the group.</p>
              <p>Drew Cleaver runs this voluntary survey. People can decide which issues to rate, and shared connections count once per issue. The results describe participating connections and show each issue’s own response count. The earlier up/down chart has a separate archive.</p>
            </details>
            <details id="north-privacy">
              <summary>Privacy and shared connections</summary>
              <p>The survey turns a connection’s public IP address into a separate private code for each issue or group. The database stores the code and the answer without the raw IP. People sharing an address can replace each other’s rating on an issue or order for a group. A changed address can count as another connection.</p>
              <p>GitHub Pages logs IP addresses for security. OpenAI Sites and Cloudflare process connection information to deliver and protect the service. Their infrastructure logs may include IP, time, route and status. The application writes no request-body or choice logs. Cloudflare can return a security-cookie header. The public survey omits credentials on every service request, so browsers neither accept nor send that cookie.</p>
              <p>This page uses no Google or ad tracking. Searches stay in this browser. Sending a suggestion or pilot lead puts it in Drew’s private review queue. A private status link lets you check the outcome. Public sharing uses only an issue’s title, question and permanent address.</p>
              {preview && <p>The private rehearsal uses its existing owner sign-in. Its ratings are separate from the public survey.</p>}
            </details>
            <details><summary>Why 45 North?</summary><p>The name borrows from Houston’s I‑45 and gives a nod to 85 South. Trump’s first term raised a question for Drew. Which changes would people living with these decisions put first?</p></details>
          </section>
        </section>
        <section id="status-view" class="status-view" hidden></section>
      </main>
      <footer class="wrap site-credit"><span>45 North</span><a href="/">{profile.name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></footer>
      <script is:inline type="application/json" id="north-catalog" set:html={JSON.stringify(seed).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c')} />
    </div>
    <script is:inline type="module" src="/45north/assets/grouped-list.mjs"></script>
  </body>
</html>
